{
 "how": "tools/lamp-viewlag.mjs, same build of the instrument on both arms. before = HEAD sources; after = Sky.updateView() split out, camera.matrixWorld refreshed in it, called from district/main.js after chase.update(). The stale arm is the opposite-reading check: the pre-fix camera body patched back in page-side on the FIXED build, with its own call counter asserted non-zero.",
 "arms": {
  "turn": "chase.update() live, the camera yawed 1.146 deg per frame from inside the frame. No sampling hole; the reading it predicts if the sky is one frame behind is exactly 1.146.",
  "drive": "chase.update() live and the camera travelling. The only arm that can see weather ordering: freeCam writes camera.position directly, so the jump arms are blind to it.",
  "jump": "freeCam to a heading 30 deg away. Isolates the stale-matrixWorld cause at a magnitude a one-frame error cannot hide in. The frame already drawn when the jump landed is excluded - it read 30 deg on the fixed build too, which is what exposed it as a hole in the instrument rather than a lag in the render.",
  "weatherJump": "kept for continuity with docs/lamp-viewlag.json. Reads a clean zero on the BROKEN build, so its zero means nothing - see drive."
 },
